#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:5
msgid "Auto Routing (Improved)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:15
msgid "What is Auto Routing (Improved) ?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:17
msgid ""
"By default, all routes must be :ref:`defined <defined-route-routing>` in "
"the configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:20
msgid ""
"However, with **Auto Routing (Improved)**, you can define the controller "
"name and its method name according to the convention and it will be "
"automatically routed. In other words, there is no need to define routes "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:24
msgid ""
"If you enable Auto Routing (Improved), when no defined route is found "
"that matches the URI, the system will attempt to match that URI against "
"the controllers and methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:28
msgid ""
"For security reasons, if a controller is used in the defined routes, Auto"
" Routing (Improved) does not route to the controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:31
msgid ""
"Auto Routing (Improved) is disabled by default. To use it, see :ref"
":`enabled-auto-routing-improved`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:36
msgid "Differences from Auto Routing (Legacy)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:38
msgid ""
":ref:`auto-routing-legacy` is a routing system from CodeIgniter 3. If you"
" are not familiar with it, go to the next section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:41
msgid ""
"If you know it well, these are some changes in **Auto Routing "
"(Improved)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:43
msgid ""
"A controller method needs HTTP verb prefix like ``getIndex()``, "
"``postCreate()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:44
msgid ""
"Since developers always know the HTTP method, a request with an "
"unexpected HTTP method will never execute the controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:46
msgid ""
"The Default Controller (``Home`` by default) and the Default Method "
"(``index`` by default) must be omitted in the URI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:47
#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:54
msgid ""
"It restricts one-to-one correspondence between controller methods and "
"URIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:48
msgid ""
"E.g. by default, you can access ``/``, but ``/home`` and ``/home/index`` "
"will be 404 Not Found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:50
msgid "It checks method parameter count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:51
msgid ""
"If there are more parameters in the URI than the method parameters, it "
"results in 404 Not Found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:53
msgid "It does not support ``_remap()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:55
msgid ""
"But it has the :ref:`auto-routing-improved-default-method-fallback` "
"feature instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:57
msgid "Can't access controllers in Defined Routes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:58
msgid ""
"It completely separates controllers accessible via **Auto Routing** from "
"those accessible via **Defined Routes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:65
msgid "Enable Auto Routing (Improved)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:67
msgid ""
"To use it, you need to change the setting ``$autoRoute`` option to "
"``true`` in **app/Config/Routing.php**::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:72
msgid ""
"And you need to change the property ``$autoRoutesImproved`` to ``true`` "
"in **app/Config/Feature.php**::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/auto_routing_improved.rst:77
msgid ""
"When you use Auto Routing (Improved), you must remove the line "
"``$routes->get('/', 'Home::index');``  in **app/Config/Routes.php**. "
"Because defined routes take precedence over Auto Routing, and controllers"
" defined in the defined routes are denied access by Auto Routing "
"(Improved) for security reasons."
msgstr ""

